WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:10.020
We, the Momoyama Predators, won our second match and are now in the quarterfinals of the district tournament.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.190
Reika-chan was in danger of dropping out of the team,

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.560
but our linkup play, along with her hard work, prevented that from happening.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.510
The eleven of us will finally play for a spot in the semifinals!

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.840
So what did your mom say after that?

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.980
Well, she's not completely for it but she's allowing me to play.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.450
It's great that you can keep on playing soccer.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.350
Yeah! You had me worried there.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.060
It's thanks to Erika-chan and everyone. Thank you all!

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.030
We didn't really do anything.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.890
This is the result of your hard work.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.060
I'm sorry.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.730
Don't worry about it! It's fine!

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:35.030
Don't mind! Don't mind!

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.940
I-I'm sorry!

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.500
D-Don't mind!

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.410
Don't mind your face!

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.270
You'll lose your captaincy like that!

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.420
How should I say this?

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.460
You could say that this isn't very gentlemanly, or not really like children.{They're not very gentlemanly. Rather, they aren't acting like children. }

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:05.360
Masaru-chan-san, as their coach, what do you think?

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.100
Not acting like children, huh?

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.440
Kota!

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.650
That was scary!

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.990
Your shot is too strong, Kota-senpai.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.190
Your job as the goalkeeper is to stop them.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.030
But!

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:39.770
That kid... He only saw my shot once or twice.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.100
He's not really acting like a child.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.200
Okay! That's all for practice! Gather around!

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.640
Tomorrow's our quarterfinal match!

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.810
Be sure to have a good night's sleep, everyone!{Rest your body properly tonight, everyone! }

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:52.810
Okay!

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:53.810
Coach!

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:58.220
We're up against Kobayashi Soccer Team next. What are they like?

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.150
I don't really know.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.550
Anyone know anything about them?

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.290
Kobayashi Soccer Team is what you call a fighting team.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:06.960
Yes, yes.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.830
Fighting team? What's that?

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:18.100
Football players need not only skill but also etiquette and emotional strength.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:22.570
All of their players practice a martial art like judo or karate.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.740
Oh? That's pretty hardcore.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.880
So all of their players are huge and impose a strong presence.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.920
They may be big, but their speed is no joke, either.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.120
So they're a strong team, right?

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.550
Oh, yes.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:38.990
Then I shall announce our lineup against them.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:43.330
It's basically the same as last time,

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:47.370
but I'm switching Ryuuji and Kota.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:53.070
So I'm a midfielder now and Kota-kun is a forward?

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:56.440
That's right. Do your best.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.580
Ryuuji, did the coach say anything to you?

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:06.520
Nope.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:10.690
The match is coming up real soon and I thought he'd say something.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.190
I don't think he's heard about that yet, right?

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.490
I don't think so.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.930
I do know from what Shou-kun said that our father talked about a lot of things.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:22.940
Then why didn't he say anything?

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:24.000
I wonder.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.110
Our last coach was only at an 
elementary school level in soccer.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:31.310
He had no real skill.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:35.110
Yeah, that's why we dropped out of the team.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:40.450
Maybe this position change is a response to that incident?

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:44.520
He wants me to fall back because of that own goal?

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.730
I don't think so.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:47.960
Why?

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.860
I'm not really certain,

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.300
but I think our coach this time isn't really worried about those kind of things.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.900
Kota-kun, don't trust in Coach Hanashima that much.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:03.240
That's right. In the end, all the adults are the same.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.880
Well, we shouldn't go all out too often.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.780
I wouldn't want to get in a fight and quit soccer again.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:13.350
I won't quit.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.760
Not until I play against him again.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:26.830
Tagi!

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.540
Okay!

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.000
Isn't that uniform a bit big for you?

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.870
This was their only size.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.940
Why Argentina?

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.380
Maradona.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:17.080
I saw a video of Maradona practicing hitting the crossbar.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.180
So you're imitating him?

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.650
Usually people aren't able to do that, though.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:24.860
My dad might be Maradona.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:29.290
Isn't your father a Spaniard?

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:32.330
They speak Spanish in Argentina, too!

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.300
It's rare to see you so into shooting practice.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.040
Momoyama Predators.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.600
Are you that concerned about them?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:44.780
They have the Demon Triplets? 
What a terrible reputation to have.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.480
But they have amazing technique.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.520
You should be able to win, Aoto.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.650
Your teammates are not bad, either.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:56.050
It's different from last year.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:07:59.960
Are you going already?

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.930
Sorry for being unable to practice with you until the end.{Sorry I'm not able to practice with you until the end. }

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:07.430
It's fine.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:12.970
Tagi.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.080
Is basketball fun?

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.380
I guess.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:56.310
Wow, they're all huge!

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:57.980
They look scary.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:04.390
Like I told you yesterday, the Momoyama Predators have the triplets as the center of their attack.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:07.160
If you suppress the three of them, you'll definitely win.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.960
Sawada! Yamaguchi! Onishi!

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:11.130
Here!

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:16.130
You three are the key! Show them 
what it means to look down on soccer!

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.640
Yes!

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:29.310
What's going on? The other team is full of muscle!

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.720
Captains, shake hands.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.660
Hey, so you're the Demon Triplets?

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.130
I heard that you three look down on soccer.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:48.300
We're the demon exterminators. Prepare yourselves.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.740
What idiotic taunts. Looks like 
something is wrong with your heads.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:57.310
Don't start pulling some martial art stunts just because you can't touch the ball.

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:58.110
What?

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.640
Say that again!

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:03.120
Hey! What are you all doing?

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.350
No fighting during the match!

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:08.690
I want you all to act like proper elementary school kids and have a fair match!

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:09.820
Y-Yes.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:11.490
We're sorry.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.860
Get into your positions.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.030
Like elementary school kids, huh. Sure, sure.

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:21.030
Jeez. We were just responding to their taunts.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:25.500
Stop right there! What did you just say?

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:26.940
Nothing, really.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.810
Just talking to ourselves.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.240
Let me make this clear to you three.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.510
If you continue your bad manners and rude play,

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.520
I shall deal with it in my own way.{I have my own ways of dealing with that. }

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.690
His own ways?

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:43.120
Go! Predators!

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.620
Go, Onii-chan!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.260
Looks like there are more spectators today.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:52.230
Onee-chan and the weird bearded old man with glasses are both here, too.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.470
Go!

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.480
They do have great strength.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:10.920
Crap!

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:17.560
Wow, what pressure.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:31.640
Hey! What's going on? Wasn't that a foul?

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:46.590
Shou!

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:47.550
Onii-chan!

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.960
I didn't think they'd come at me directly.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:54.890
Where's the ball!?

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:02.030
Crap!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.740
That was a foul?

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.710
Hehe, lucky.

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:11.940
He didn't blow his whistle then, but now he does?

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.080
It's going over there!

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:13.780
All right!

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.350
Ouzou-kun!

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.260
This time I'll...

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.360
Yes!

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.170
Again!?

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.500
Crap!

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:42.970
Faster! I must be faster! Next time I'll break loose!

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.860
Aren't they getting pushed back?

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:03.730
Hmm, if I put the difference in their strength and weight on a graph...

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:07.400
You can see how desperate the situation is.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.740
Going man-to-man will just result in them getting pummeled.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:13.870
The only way for this to change will be...

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.340
Big Tri!

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.840
Yes! Good decision!

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:21.550
Mark him!

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:31.260
Ryuuji-kun and Kota-kun are being marked!

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:37.030
Are these guys planning on isolating the three of us?

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:57.050
Huh? A yellow card!?

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.780
Hey, this has to be a joke.{Hey, this isn't a joke. }

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:02.290
Ouzou-kun, did you trip him up?

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:05.820
No. He fell by himself.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.260
I see.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:10.600
This is what he meant by having his own ways.

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.200
You only blow your whistle at us!? This is refball!

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.600
Hey! It's unfair!

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:19.570
Watch your manners, old man.
 I can kick you out any time I want!

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:28.310
Your team didn't really play the beautiful game, am I right?

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.820
More like, they didn't play like gentlemen...

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.490
Now I see.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.130
Crap!

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.560
Yes! He got past!

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.780
Wait!

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.390
You elbowed me on purpose, didn't you?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.660
What did you say?

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.890
You got proof?

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:13.860
Quit playing dumb.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:15.530
What? You wanna go?

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:18.400
Hey! Over there! What are you doing? Stop it!

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.000
Stop it, Kota!

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.730
Calm down, Kota-kun.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:31.010
Eh? Only Kota-kun?

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:32.040
No way.

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:36.110
What's with that attitude?

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:37.950
Are you mad at my decisions?

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.820
No, we are not.

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:42.390
Sorry for the ruckus.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.760
You should understand by now.

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:49.960
That referee is trying to run us out of this game.

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:54.630
If you go against him and get kicked out, then you've fallen right into his hands.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:58.300
In any case, the only thing we can do is lie low for a while.

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:00.370
Kota-kun, are you okay?

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.070
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:05.980
In any case, Shou! We're being marked too tightly so we can't do anything.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:10.720
We'll fall back. You have to call other players to go forward.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:12.520
Okay. I understand.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:19.490
I think our man-marking is working better than expected.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.890
Yeah. It's like the referee is on our side.

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:25.800
Now the triplets can't do anything.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:27.630
This match is ours!

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.110
Why are you getting scared?

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.620
Don't go one-on-one! Pass before they get close!

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:55.830
Erika-chan! Uematsu-kun! Uchimura-kun! Ukishima-kun!

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:57.600
Remember our match against Rosa!

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.030
Oh yeah.

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:05.440
We practiced quick passing because of the size difference.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.590
Oh, so close!

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:28.090
Fall back! Strengthen the defense!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:02.130
I just want to say one thing.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:05.060
You guys are strong.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:09.330
Just play your own style of soccer. You'll definitely win.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:14.170
Don't feel down! Bring out your confidence!

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:20.010
That last attack wasn't bad.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:23.750
Yeah. If we pass a bit faster, we'll definitely link up more.

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:26.350
We'll definitely score in the second half!

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:27.220
Yeah!

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:29.890
Kota! Ryuuji! Ouzou!

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.790
You guys have been keeping a low profile.{You've become quite settled. }

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:37.000
What's wrong? You can't get past that level of marking?

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:42.130
Well, it's more like the referee has got his eyes on us.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:44.940
For the sake of the team, we don't to get kicked out of the game.{We don't want to get kicked out of the game for the team's sake. }

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:48.070
We're delinquents, in the end.

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:52.210
Our last coach also told us to play more like elementary school kids.

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:57.850
Who are you playing against? The referee? The coach?

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:03.420
I've never told any of you 
to play like elementary school kids.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:06.560
I told you to play your own soccer.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:10.260
Just show us your unique brand of soccer.

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:14.230
Because <i>you</i> are the ones playing on the pitch.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:21.310
This coach is really a bit different.{I think this coach is truly a bit different. }

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:24.240
Our own unique brand of soccer, huh?

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:28.580
Well, now that the coach has given us permission, let's just roll with it.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:29.680
Okay!

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:02.810
W-Who's who!?

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.020
They're so fast! I can't tell!

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:11.160
Weren't you supposed to mark Ryuuji?

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.930
Let me knock you out again!

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:24.140
Again? This is the first time for me, though.

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:40.650
Our own soccer, right?

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.030
What's the matter?

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:50.700
We scored.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:53.530
Was that against the rules?

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:01.340
Yes!

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:02.210
The first goal!

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:09.850
Yes! That's it! Just keep on scoring!

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:23.060
That's the second yellow card. 
You know what that means, right?

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:24.660
What are you talking about?

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:25.360
What?

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:29.870
This is my first yellow card, unless I'm remembering things wrong.

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:33.340
Oh no, sorry.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.570
All right!

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:40.140
Go, Onii-chan!

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:42.080
Uematsu-kun, pass!

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.780
Got it!

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:51.960
Nice!

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:55.390
The Demon Triplets, huh?

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:02.900
Thank you very much!

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:06.140
Yes! They won!

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:07.270
Congratulations!

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:12.280
You told me that the kids didn't play gentlemanly soccer, right?

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:16.250
Was that refereeing gentlemanly, I wonder?

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:17.980
Oh... No.

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:19.550
Oh... No.

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:24.390
We'll be issuing a formal complaint about the officiating for this match.

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:25.590
Excuse me.

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:35.600
Masaru-chan-san.

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:38.570
Here are the videos for the three matches so far.

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:42.240
I thought you'd understand this time.

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.010
Please use these as learning tools.

00:22:58.160 --> 00:23:00.760
Now then, what should I do?

00:24:35.620 --> 00:24:38.690
Wow, the Furuyas are so popular!

00:24:38.690 --> 00:24:40.760
Well, they do look that way.

00:24:40.760 --> 00:24:42.560
Coach Hanashima took a break from practice...

00:24:42.560 --> 00:24:44.900
...and went to check out the Chiba Thunderbolts.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:47.260
Is he trying to give the triplets a hard time?

00:24:47.260 --> 00:24:50.470
No way... Actually, you're right!

00:24:50.470 --> 00:24:52.400
Next episode of Ginga e Kickoff!!

00:24:52.400 --> 00:24:54.070
Own Goal.
